    "diagnosis": "<p>Low-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion (LSIL)</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>LSIL (anal intraepithelial neoplasia&nbsp;I [AIN&nbsp;I]) is characterized by koilocytosis with hyperchromatic raisinoid nuclei and perinuclear haloes. Dyskeratosis is noted. There are no atypical mitoses.</p>",
    "source": "Rondell P. Graham",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/70/555.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/70/thumb_555.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32128,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 70,
    "fileId": 561,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>High-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion (HSIL)</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>HSIL (anal intraepithelial neoplasia&nbsp;III [AIN&nbsp;III]) shows full-thickness mucosal involvement by hyperchromatic cells with a high N:C&nbsp;ratio. Mitotic figures, including atypical forms, are seen in the upper two&nbsp;thirds of the mucosa.</p>",
    "source": "Rondell P. Graham",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/70/561.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/70/thumb_561.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32129,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 70,
    "fileId": 565,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Basaloid high-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion (HSIL)</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>HSIL may show a basaloid morphology characterized by full-thickness involvement by immature-appearing hyperchromatic cells. Cases may show an admixture of basaloid and warty HSIL.</p>",
    "source": "Rondell P. Graham",
